A reference goes in, a reference comes out. That is the whole shape of it. `deref` never builds a new value, it only re-borrows the one that is already sitting somewhere, taking a shorter path to it. So a chain of coercion steps can only start from a reference, because there is no step that could take an owned value and turn it into one.

