--- README.md ---
# agent-pipeline

The backend team's researcher, coder and reviewer agents for small backend tickets.
Label a ticket `agent-ok` and the worker picks it up: the researcher reads the
ticket, the code and any vendor docs; the coder makes the change on a branch;
the reviewer reviews it. When the reviewer approves, the run comments on the
ticket with the branch, and an engineer opens the PR.

Channel: #agent-pipeline. Models run through the internal LLM
gateway, llm-gw.

## How a run works

```
orchestrator -> researcher -> summarizer -> coder <-> reviewer -> orchestrator
```

- Agents only talk through messages (`AgentMessage` in `src/types.ts`). The
  coordinator in `src/pipeline.ts` is plain code, not an LLM: it routes each
  message to the agent it is addressed to and builds that agent's input from
  the message log.
- The summarizer condenses the researcher's notes into a short brief, so the
  coder's context stays small (`handoff.maxWords` in `pipeline.config.json`).
- The reviewer can send a change back to the coder at most
  `review.maxRevisionRounds` times; after that the run is escalated to a human.
- A finished run writes `runs/<runId>/messages.json`: every message, the config
  the run used, and token and tool-call totals.

## Agents

| Agent | Model | Tools | Prompt |
|---|---|---|---|
| researcher | model-2 | fetch_url, search_code, read_file | prompts/researcher.md |
| summarizer | model-2-mini | none | prompts/summarizer.md |
| coder | model-2 | read_file, write_file, run_tests | prompts/coder.md |
| reviewer | model-2 | none | prompts/reviewer.md |

Tools run inside llm-gw, against a checkout of the target repo on the branch
`agent/<ticket>-r<runId>`. The pipeline only sees each agent's final text and
its usage (tokens, tool calls, time).

## Running it

Node 22.18 or later runs the TypeScript directly; there is no build step.

```
npm install
node src/run.ts TRK-1482      # one ticket, in the foreground
npm run worker               # the service: polls the tracker for agent-ok tickets
npm test
```

The worker runs up to `WORKER_CONCURRENCY` pipelines at once (default 4) in one
Node process, and abandons a run after `RUN_TIMEOUT_MS` (default 20 minutes).

Environment: `LLM_GATEWAY_URL`, `LLM_GATEWAY_TOKEN`, `TRACKER_URL`,
`TRACKER_TOKEN`.

