- `body: Box<Item>` in `Section`
- `Sub(Box<Section>)` in `Item`

That way the recursive parts become pointers with a known fixed size.

The Box could also go the other way around on one of the links, as long as only one side of each recursive step is indirect. For example, you could box the `Section` inside `Sub`, or box the `Item` inside `body`; the key is breaking the cycle with an indirection.

`List(Vec<Item>)` needs no Box because `Vec` itself is a fixed-size handle. It stores its items on the heap, so the `Item` type only needs to know the size of the `Vec`, not the size of all its elements inline.
