With `Result<i32, Box<dyn Error>>`, the caller can’t easily tell whether the failure was a timeout or bad data, because both get erased behind the trait object. The fix is to use a concrete error enum, for example `LoadError::Timeout` and `LoadError::BadData`, so the loop can match on the error and retry only timeouts.

`Box<dyn Error>` is still useful when you want to return different error types from one function and you don’t need the caller to branch on the exact kind, just display or propagate it.
