There are two bugs in the second file.

1) The loop removes elements while iterating forward with `for i in 0..items.len()`. After a removal, all later elements shift left, so the next index can be skipped. That means it can miss some values that should be removed.

2) The range length is decided before the loop starts. Since `items.len()` changes after removals, the loop can still try to access an index that is now out of bounds, which can panic.

A simple fix is to build a new list of the values to keep, then replace the old one. No closures needed.
