This panics while iterating. The first bug is removing from a `Vec` using a forward index loop (`for i in 0..items.len()`), which causes later elements to shift left; then the loop still advances `i`, so some elements get skipped and the indexing can go out of sync. The second bug is that `items.len()` is evaluated once at the start of the range, so the loop bounds don’t adjust as items are removed. A simple fix is to build a new vector by walking the items and keeping only the ones at or below 5.
