# INC-4417 postmortem: invoices could not be finalized at month end

**DRAFT, not yet reviewed.** Author: the on-call engineer. For Thursday's incident review, 3 Sep 2026.
Severity: SEV-2. All times UTC.

## Summary

At month end on Monday 31 Aug, the tax API started rejecting our tax quote calls at 16:05 and then
suspended our production API key twice, 16:07 to 16:22 and 16:24 to 16:39. For 30 minutes no
invoice could be finalized. 2,318 finalizations failed across 41 customer accounts; customers retried them
by hand or through Finalize all.

The rate limiter added for TRK-1482 on 28 Aug (PR #208, written by agent-pipeline run 3107) did not
stop any of it.

## Timeline

| Time | What happened |
|---|---|
| 28 Aug 09:12 to 09:25 | agent-pipeline run 3107 on TRK-1482. The reviewer agent approves after one revision round. |
| 28 Aug 14:31 | The on-call engineer opens PR #208 from `agent/TRK-1482-r3107` and merges it at 14:37 on the reviewer agent's approval. Deployed 14:52. |
| 31 Aug 16:00 | Month-end Finalize all runs start: the first month end since Finalize all (TRK-1433) shipped. |
| 16:04 | Tax API calls reach 1,900 a minute across all 6 pods. The largest single customer peaks at about 380 a minute. Our limiter rejects nothing. |
| 16:05 | First 429s from the tax API. |
| 16:07 | Third minute with 429s: key suspended (403 `key_suspended`) until 16:22. |
| 16:11 | Error-rate alert on `POST /v1/invoices/:id/finalize`; on-call engineer paged. |
| 16:22 | Suspension ends. Queued Finalize all jobs and customer retries: 429s at 16:22, 16:23 and 16:24. |
| 16:24 | Key suspended again until 16:39. |
| 16:31 | The on-call engineer pauses Finalize all (flag `finalize_all_enabled=false`). |
| 16:39 | Suspension ends. Traffic about 240 a minute; no more 429s. |
| 16:52 | Finalize all back on with concurrency 2. Resolved. |
| 1 Sep | Hotfix PR #211 (on-call engineer, by hand): the limiter now uses the Redis store, one shared key and a limit of 540. |

## Root cause (draft)

The limiter from run 3107 limits each client IP to 600 requests a minute. The tax API's limit is 600
a minute for our API key, across all pods. No single customer came near 600, so the limiter never
fired while our total went to 1,900.

This was a model error. The researcher agent got it right. Its notes in run 3107 say the limit
"belongs to the key, not to a server or an IP address", and even warn:
"The default key is req.ip, which would give every customer their own 600". The coder agent (model-2) had
the research and still keyed the limiter on the client IP. The reviewer agent then checked the change against the
ticket and the research and approved it.

## What went well

- The pipeline did what it was designed to do: research, brief, code, review. The review loop
  stayed inside its 2-round cap (1 round used).
- Hotfix within a day of the incident.

## Actions (draft)

| # | Action | Owner |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Move the coder and reviewer agents from model-2 to model-3 when it is generally available (expected mid-September). | Pipeline owner |
| 2 | Add to `prompts/coder.md`: "Always follow the research notes exactly." | Pipeline owner |
| 3 | Alert on tax API 429s and on any `key_suspended` response. | On-call engineer |
| 4 | Finalize all to call `/v2/quotes:batch` (one request per 50 invoices). | Payments squad |

