--- README.md ---
# onboarding-form

The supplier onboarding form. It is rendered from a JSON schema served by the
forms API (`GET /api/forms/supplier-onboarding`), so the business can add or
change fields without a release.

- Schema version 14: 312 fields in 9 sections. 103 fields have a `showIf` rule
  and appear only when another answer has a given value.
- `schema/onboarding.sample.json` holds the first two sections (Company
  details, Tax). The other seven sections use the same field types.
- A user's answers are saved as a draft (`GET /api/drafts/current`) and sent on
  submit.
- Fields with `"validate": "vat"` are checked by the validation API
  (`GET /api/validate/vat?value=...&country=...`) as the user types.

`src/App.tsx` is the entry component. The host page loads the schema and the
draft and renders `<App>`.

## Layout

```
src/
  App.tsx                     the entry component
  api/validate.ts             client for the validation API
  form/
    types.ts                  schema and value types
    FormProvider.tsx          form state and the context
    FormRenderer.tsx          sections and fields from the schema
    Field.tsx                 one field: label, input, help, error
    visibility.ts             showIf rules
    useRemoteValidation.ts    debounced server-side checks
    debounce.ts
schema/
  onboarding.sample.json
```

## Run

```
npm install
npm run dev
```

