--- README.md ---
# telemetryd

Reads two ADC channels, stores every frame in a telemetry file as a 64-byte
record with a CRC, and sends over-range events and a periodic status line as
UDP datagrams.

Target: the data logger board, 4 x Cortex-A72 (aarch64), Linux 6.6, glibc.
The previous board (2 x Cortex-A9, 32-bit armhf) runs the same source.

## Threads

| Thread | Code | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `cap0`, `cap1` | `capture.c` | one per channel: `read(2)` one frame from `/dev/tlm_adcN` (2000 frames/s), build the record in place in the channel's ring, count it |
| `writer` | `writer.c` | drain both rings, check each record's CRC, write 64 records per `write(2)` |
| `uplink` | `uplink.c` | send queued event messages as UDP datagrams, give each buffer back to the pool |
| `status` | `stats.c` | every `status_period_ms`: print the counters; every `status_uplink_every` periods, queue a status datagram |

What they share:

- capture to writer: one ring per channel (`ring.c`), one producer and one
  consumer each, lock-free;
- capture and status to uplink: message buffers from `msgpool.c` (lock-free),
  queued to the uplink thread under a mutex (`uplink.c`);
- every thread: the counters in `g_stats` (`stats.h`) and the configuration
  (`config.c`, loaded on first use).

## Record (`record.h`)

| Field | Bytes | |
|---|---|---|
| `seq` | 4 | per channel, from 0; a dropped frame leaves a gap |
| `channel`, `nsamples` | 2 + 2 | |
| `t_ns` | 8 | `CLOCK_MONOTONIC` of the first sample |
| `samples` | 40 | 20 x int16 |
| `flags` | 4 | `TLM_FLAG_OVERRANGE` |
| `crc` | 4 | CRC-32 of the 60 bytes before it |

## Build

    make                                     # host
    make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu-    # board

## Configuration

`/etc/telemetryd.conf` (or the file named by `TLM_CONFIG`), `key = value`:
`adc_dev0`, `adc_dev1`, `out_path`, `uplink_host`, `uplink_port`,
`status_period_ms` (1000), `status_uplink_every` (10).

## Tests

Host tests, run on developer machines:

    make test                  # ring_stress, stats_check, msgpool_stress
    make SANITIZE=thread test  # under ThreadSanitizer (clang)

- `ring_stress`: one producer and one consumer push 20M records through a
  ring as fast as they can; every record must come out with the right `seq`
  and a good CRC.
- `stats_check`: runs `capture_emit()`, `writer_drain()` and the status thread
  with known input and compares `g_stats` with what the threads did.
- `msgpool_stress`: three threads take and give back message buffers; a
  buffer must never be handed to two threads, and all 64 must be back in the
  pool at the end.

--- src/capture.c ---
/* capture.c - one thread per ADC channel: read frames, build records, push */
#include <errno.h>
#include <fcntl.h>
#include <inttypes.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <unistd.h>

#include "config.h"
#include "msgpool.h"
#include "stats.h"
#include "telemetryd.h"

static void post_overrange(const struct tlm_rec *rec)
{
	struct msg *m = msgpool_get();
	int n;

	if (m == NULL) {
		stats_inc(&g_stats.events_dropped);
		return;
	}
	n = snprintf((char *)m->data, sizeof(m->data),
		     "overrange ch=%u seq=%" PRIu32 " t_ns=%" PRIu64,
		     rec->channel, rec->seq, rec->t_ns);
	m->len = (uint16_t)(n < (int)sizeof(m->data) ? n : (int)sizeof(m->data) - 1);
	uplink_post(m);
}

bool capture_emit(struct capture *c, const struct adc_frame *f)
{
	struct tlm_rec *rec = ring_reserve(c->ring);
	struct tlm_rec ev;

	if (rec == NULL) {
		c->seq++;			/* keep the gap visible in the file */
		stats_inc(&g_stats.dropped);
		return false;
	}
	rec->seq = c->seq++;
	rec->channel = (uint16_t)c->channel;
	rec->nsamples = TLM_REC_SAMPLES;
	rec->t_ns = f->t_ns;
	memcpy(rec->samples, f->samples, sizeof(rec->samples));
	rec->flags = f->flags;
	rec->crc = tlm_rec_crc(rec);
	ev = *rec;
	ring_commit(c->ring);
	stats_inc(&g_stats.captured);

	if (ev.flags & TLM_FLAG_OVERRANGE)
		post_overrange(&ev);
	return true;
}

void *capture_thread(void *arg)
{
	struct capture *c = arg;
	const struct tlm_config *cfg = config_get();
	struct adc_frame f;

	c->fd = open(cfg->adc_dev[c->channel], O_RDONLY);
	if (c->fd < 0) {
		fprintf(stderr, "telemetryd: %s: %s\n",
			cfg->adc_dev[c->channel], strerror(errno));
		return NULL;
	}

	while (!g_stop) {
		ssize_t n = read(c->fd, &f, sizeof(f));	/* blocks until the next frame */

		if (n == (ssize_t)sizeof(f))
			capture_emit(c, &f);
		else if (n < 0 && errno != EINTR)
			break;
	}
	close(c->fd);
	return NULL;
}

