### Drop label comes from the value · 2 Nov

### Drop label vs variable name

The text printed by `Tracer`'s drop comes from the string passed to `Tracer(...)` when the value was built, not from the variable that owns it at drop time.

```rust
let a = Tracer("a");
let b = a;            // move: b is the owner now, a is dead
// at the end of the scope this prints `drop a`, not `drop b`
```

One value, one drop, under the label it was born with. The variable name never appears in the output.

