I’d fix it by preloading the calibration data once for the shipment’s sensors, or by joining/calculating it in one query. For example: fetch the shipment with its readings, collect the distinct SensorIds, load the relevant calibrations in one query, then do the version selection in memory; or better, reshape the query so EF can translate it into a single SQL statement. I’d also add an index on SensorCalibrations (SensorId, ValidFrom desc) if it isn’t already there.

