There are two bugs in `p2.rs`.

1) The loop uses `for i in 0..items.len()`, but `items.len()` changes when you call `remove`. That means indices can shift while the loop still keeps going, so it may skip elements and can also try to access an index that no longer exists.

2) Even before that, removing while iterating forward over indices is logically wrong here: after removing an element, everything after it moves left, but `i` still increases. So some elements never get checked. In this example, `8` gets removed, then `9` shifts left into its place, but the loop moves on and misses it.

A correct fix is to use a `while` loop and only advance the index when you do not remove an element.

