`fn drop(&mut self)` takes a `&mut Holder`: a mutable reference to the whole struct. Rust has no such thing as a reference to a half-moved value. Once `h.label` has been moved out, `h` is no longer a complete `Holder`, so no `&mut Holder` can exist, and `drop` cannot be called at all. It is not only that `drop` might look at the missing field. It could never get a valid `self` in the first place.

