### add_both contract vs arms · 2 Nov

**add_both: the contract decides, not Option**

`Option` is just `enum Option<T> { Some(T), None }`. It has no built-in rule for combining two values, so nothing about it says whether `Some` plus `None` keeps the value or gives up.

The rule comes from the doc comment on `add_both` (ex2_options.rs lines 12-13): "The sum when both are present, otherwise None". A sum needs two numbers, so one number alone is `None`.

My arm `(Some(x), None) => Some(x)` breaks that contract. The test on line 41, `assert_eq!(add_both(Some(2), None), None);`, expects `None`.

Lesson: read the doc comment as the spec, and check each match arm against it.

