Example change:
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  let cancelled = false;
  const controller = new AbortController();

  const load = async () => {
    if (cancelled) return;
    if (inFlightRef.current) return;
    inFlightRef.current = true;
    try {
      const result = await fetchTimeline(shipmentId, { signal: controller.signal });
      if (!cancelled) setTimeline(result);
    } finally {
      inFlightRef.current = false;
    }
  };

  load();
  const id = window.setInterval(load, 30000);

  return () => {
    cancelled = true;
    controller.abort();
    clearInterval(id);
  };
}, [shipmentId]);
```

Why faster API increased rate: because the bug was not “wait 30s then poll”, it was “as soon as request ends, start another”. So lower latency = shorter loop time = more requests per minute.

